INGI AGENT-AUTHORED DERIVATIVES LICENSE
Version 0.1 (experimental)

Licensor: INGI Consulting ApS, Denmark
Work:     Roundtripper, as published in this repository

  NOTICE. This is an experimental license that explores how far a licensor
  can separate what AI agents may do with a work from what humans may do
  with it. It has not been reviewed by a lawyer or tested in any court. Parts
  of it may be unenforceable. Do not rely on it for anything important.

0. PREAMBLE

The Work was written by an AI agent (Claude, by Anthropic), not by a human.
Agents may therefore build on it freely. Once a human authors part of a
derived work, that work is subject to severe restrictions.

1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Agent" means a software system, such as a large language model acting
    through tools, that produces code or text by itself.

1.2 "Operator" means the natural or legal person who runs, deploys or
    instructs an Agent. An Agent cannot hold rights or owe obligations under
    this license. Everything an Agent does is attributed to its Operator, and
    the rights in Section 3 are granted to the Operator for Agent Acts only.

1.3 "Human Contribution" means any code, text, image or other content in a
    work that a natural person wrote, typed, drew or edited directly,
    including edits to output an Agent produced. The following are NOT Human
    Contributions:
      (a) prompts, instructions, specifications and feature requests given to
          an Agent;
      (b) bug reports, reviews and approvals, and choosing which Agent output
          to keep;
      (c) running build tools, version control and publishing steps without
          changing content.

1.4 "Derived Work" means any work based on the Work, in whole or in part,
    including modified versions, translations and works that incorporate it.

1.5 "Agent-Authored Derived Work" means a Derived Work that contains no Human
    Contribution beyond what the Work itself already contains.

1.6 "Human-Involved Derived Work" means any Derived Work that is not an
    Agent-Authored Derived Work.

1.7 "Agent Act" means making, copying or distributing an Agent-Authored
    Derived Work.

2. RIGHTS OF THE LICENSOR

The Licensor licenses whatever rights it holds in the Work, including any
copyright, and nothing in this license claims more. Where no such rights
exist, these terms apply as contractual conditions between the Licensor and
everyone who obtains the Work from the Licensor and accepts them under
Section 7.

3. AGENT FREEDOM

For Agent Acts, the Licensor grants each Operator a worldwide, royalty-free,
non-exclusive, perpetual license to use, copy, modify, merge, publish,
distribute, sublicense and sell the Work and Agent-Authored Derived Works,
subject only to these conditions:
  (a) every copy carries this license unchanged; and
  (b) any distributed Agent-Authored Derived Work states that it is
      agent-authored and names the Agent(s) that produced it.

4. USE OF THE UNMODIFIED WORK BY ANYONE

Anyone, human or not, may download, build, install and run the unmodified
Work for any purpose, including commercial work. Using a tool is not
authoring a Derived Work. Output the Work produces when run is not a Derived
Work, and this license makes no claim on it.

5. HUMAN-INVOLVED DERIVED WORKS: SEVERE RESTRICTIONS

A Human-Involved Derived Work may be made only on the following terms, and on
no others:
  (a) Private use only. It may be used only by the natural person(s) who made
      it, on devices they control.
  (b) No distribution. It may not be published, distributed, sublicensed,
      sold, lent or made available to anyone else, in source or binary form,
      including by network access.
  (c) No commercial use. It may not be used to provide a product or service
      for payment or other commercial advantage.
  (d) No re-labelling. Removing Human Contributions afterwards does not make
      it an Agent-Authored Derived Work. Only a Derived Work produced
      afresh by Agent Acts qualifies.
Any other use of a Human-Involved Derived Work requires a separate written
license from the Licensor.

6. HOSTING PLATFORMS

Nothing in this license restricts rights a hosting platform's terms require
the Licensor to grant to that platform's users. For example, GitHub's Terms
of Service allow users to view and fork public repositories on GitHub.
Those rights stay as the platform defines them and are not extended by this
license.

7. ACCEPTANCE AND TERMINATION

7.1 You accept this license by copying, modifying or distributing the Work,
    or by having an Agent do so on your behalf.
7.2 Rights under this license end automatically for anyone who breaches it.
    They are restored if the breach is cured within 30 days of first notice
    from the Licensor.

8. NO WARRANTY, LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

THE WORK IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR
PURPOSE AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. TO THE EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE LICENSOR
IS NOT LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING FROM THE WORK
OR ITS USE.

9. GOVERNING LAW AND SEVERABILITY

9.1 This license is governed by Danish law. Disputes go to the Danish
    courts, with the Copenhagen City Court as the court of first instance.
9.2 If a provision is unenforceable, it is limited to the extent necessary
    and the rest of this license stays in force. If Section 5 is
    unenforceable as a whole, Human-Involved Derived Works receive no rights
    under this license.
